  "visualDNA": {
    "Overview": "It is characterized by its green color and blue cracks on the surface. Much of it is multi-layered. Because the ma in sōma means \"horse\", calligraphic horses are painted on many pieces, often as a stylized horse painted in metallic gold. A very rare character of Sōma ware is its multi-layered structure. The dual layering of the pottery insulates the hot liquids to keep them hot and keeps the outside cool, so one doesn't burn one's hands."
  },
